WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.180
So with that, we can open up the�

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:02.880
we can open the line for questions, Sharon.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:04.540
Thank you.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.860
To ask a question,

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.800
you will need to press star one and one on your telephone

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.420
and wait for your name to be announced.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.680
Please limit yourself to one question

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.780
and return to the queue for any follow-up.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.380
To withdraw your question, please press star one and one.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.460
We will now go to our first question.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.160
And the first question today comes from the line of Peter Fadolt

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.280
from BNP Paribas.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.260
Please go ahead.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.150
Yeah, thanks, Peter Fadolt, BNP.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.310
Just one question, just a deep dive, please, Vaz, on HS.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.510
Could you perhaps talk about MBRX during the presentation,

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.190
but could you talk about current volume price dynamics

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.250
for Cosentix in HS,

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:46.750
the target clinical profile for Rapsido in HS,

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.790
and how, if the data is positive,

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.530
you would intend to position both assets in the market?

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:51.950
Thank you.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.810
Yeah, Peter, absolutely.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.690
So overall, you know, with Cosentix,

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:59.250
we've had stable, I'd say, gross to net

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.150
across our indication suite.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.950
This year.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.810
So I think we've been able to manage things pretty well.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:09.010
So overall, you know, with this is primarily,

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:12.910
we saw very solid volume growth in the quarter with HS.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.910
More of the headwinds that we saw

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.710
were with some of the older indications.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:21.450
But nothing notable in terms of increased gross to nets

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.570
for Cosentix in the quarter.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.710
And when you think about remibrutinib,

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.470
the phase two data indicated, I think, impressive,

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.130
well, early, but impressive,

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.410
results in disease management.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.030
I think we'll ultimately have to see

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.610
how the phase three results play out.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.370
But the ambition would be to play,

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:43.050
as we have remibrutinib in CSU and plantidu and syndu,

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.450
is to hopefully have an oral option

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.710
that could be placed ahead of biologics.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:51.690
And so clearly having two medicines would be helpful.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.070
We would have the oral option

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:55.630
and ultimately the biologic option as well.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.310
But I think this is really dependent on the data set.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:00.250
This is a heterogeneous population,

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.130
and we're going to have to do a lot of work on that.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:02.170
We're going to have to see how the data looks

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.390
before we can fully define the positioning.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:06.330
Next question.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.350
Thank you.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.490
Your next question comes from the line of

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.230
Sachin Jain from Bank of America.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.210
Please go ahead.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.050
Hi there.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.230
I actually have a follow-on to the prior question,

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.050
NHS, if I may.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.310
So you sort of commented that,

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.150
but what's your target efficacy profile

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.550
relative to existing biologics?

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.190
Just given the phase two was hard to interpret

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.670
with the inverse dose response and varied placebo,

